{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom:0cm;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\nmso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-bidi-font-weight:\r\nbold&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;The proposed rear extension, in conjunction with the gable ended large\r\nrear dormer roof extensions, would introduce an incongruous, overly dominant\r\nand obtrusive form of development that would fail to respect the form and\r\nproportions of the existing building, and the character and appearance of\r\nneighbouring properties, to the detriment of the character and appearance of\r\nthe existing dwellinghouse and the surrounding area, contrary to the high\r\nquality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2023),\r\nPolicy D3.D (1) and (11) of The London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1B of the\r\nHarrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the Harrow Development Management\r\nPolicies Local Plan (2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document\r\nResidential Design Guide (2010).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom:0cm;mso-add-space:auto;\r\ntext-align:justify;text-indent:-18.0pt;line-height:normal;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;\r\nmso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:\r\n&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-bidi-font-weight:\r\nbold&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;The proposal, by reason of the poor and cramped layout, poor outlook from\r\nhabitable rooms and the failure to demonstrate adequate internal storage areas\r\nwould result in a poor standard of living accommodation for future occupiers to\r\nthe detriment of their residential amenities, contrary to the National Planning\r\nPolicy Framework (2023), Policies D6 and D3 (D.7 and D.10) of The London Plan\r\n(2021), Policies DM1 and DM26 of the Harrow Development Management Policies\r\nLocal Plan (2013), The Mayor of London Housing Supplementary Planning Guidance\r\n(2016), the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide\r\n(2010) and Housing Design Standards LPG (2023).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;The proposed development,\r\nby reason of the cumulative width and height of the rear extension would appear\r\noverbearing and visually obtrusive, and would result in undue loss of outlook,\r\nloss of privacy and sense of enclosure to the detriment of the residential\r\namenities of neighbouring occupiers at Nos. 52/54 Station Road, contrary to the\r\nNational Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policy D3 (D.7) of The London Plan\r\n(2021), Policy CS1 of Harrow&#x27;s Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the\r\nDevelopment Management Policies Local Plan document (2013) and the relevant\r\nprovisions of the adopted Harrow Supplementary Planning Document Residential\r\nDesign Guide (2010).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
